{
  "title": "Patellar Clunk Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/5024/patellar-clunk-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 11 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Patellar Clunk Syndrome is a painful, palpable \"clunk\" that can occur at the patellofemoral articulation of a posterior stabilized TKA caused by a fibrous nodule of scar tissue.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with the presence of a painful, palpable \"pop\" or \"catch\" as knee extends (~40° of flexion).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation for patients with mild symptoms. Surgical resection of the fibrous nodule is indicated for patients with severe symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "prevalence reported at 3.5%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "even less frequent with newer component designs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "preoperative factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "preop patella baja",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "valgus pre-operative alignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "preoperative fibrosynovial proliferation at quadriceps insertion into superior pole of patella",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "resect this at the time of surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "previous knee surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**component factors**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patellar component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**small patellar** component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "because of decreased quads tendon contact forces against superior aspect of intercondylar box, allowing fibrosynovial proliferation and entrapment in intercondylar region of the box",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patellar component placed **low** on the patella",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "exposes unresurfaced superior pole and quadriceps tendon to contact with femoral component",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patellar **overresection** and thin patellar button",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "reduces **offset** of quadriceps tendon from top of trochler groove",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "exposure of cut patellar bone that is not covered by patellar component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "resect uncovered lateral patellar facet",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**femoral component**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**PS design**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "increased posterior femoral condylar **offset**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "smaller femoral component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "femoral component in flexed position",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "causes by more posterior entry point for intramedullary distal femoral cutting jig, because of anterior bow of femur",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "femoral component with higher intercondylar box ratio (trochlear groove extended more proximal and anterior)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "thick polyethylene insert",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "raises joint line, creates relative patella baja",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "A painful, palpable \"clunk\" at the patellofemoral articulation of **posterior stabilized TKA** caused by a fibrous nodule of scar tissue at the posterior surface of the distal quadriceps tendon/superior patellar pole catching on the box of the femoral component during knee extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cause of scar tissue is unknown, but may be related to:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "direct trauma to quadriceps tendon during patella resection during TKA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "impingement of the quadriceps tendon on the femoral component due to an undersized patellar component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "scar is entrapped within the intercondylar notch during flexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the scar is forced out of the notch during active knee extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the painful snap or clunk is usually felt between 30-45 degrees",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presents an average of 12 months after TKA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patellofemoral knee pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "complaints of knee \"popping\" and \"catching\"",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "painful, palpable **\"pop\" or \"catch\" as knee extends (~40° of flexion)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "US",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "shows suprapatellar fibrous tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Patellar crunch syndrome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs when scar accumulates around the patellar component, causing a crunching sensation when bringing the knee from extension to flexion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic vs open resection of fibrous nodule",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/5024/images/nodulepic.jpg",
                  "caption": "Arthroscopic image of a knee with patellar clunk syndrome"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/5024/images/afterscope.jpg",
                  "caption": "Arthroscopic resection of fibrous knee nodule causing patellar clunk syndrome"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes of arthroscopic resection are good, with very low rates of recurrence and improvement in knee society scores",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
